    "collapsible_content_nJrYmE": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "How is this different from the Heimlich maneuver?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/> While the Heimlich maneuver is the standard first step in a choking emergency, it may not always be effective—especially if you are alone, physically unable to perform it, or dealing with a stubborn obstruction. This device uses a powerful, targeted suction mechanism to safely dislodge objects in seconds when traditional methods fail.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Is this a professional medical device?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/>This is a non-prescription, household first-aid device. It is designed to be completely safe and easy for anyone to operate in an emergency. However, it is an emergency backup tool and does not replace the need to call emergency services immediately.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Who is this device designed for?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/> It is designed to protect your entire family! Every kit comes with three different mask sizes (Small, Medium, Large), making it perfectly suitable for young children, adults, and seniors.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Does it require batteries or charging?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/>Not at all. The device is 100% manual and mechanically operated. You never have to worry about dead batteries or finding a charger in a critical, life-threatening moment. Just place the mask and press the button to activate the suction.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Can it accidentally push the object further down?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/>No, it is built with a specially designed bidirectional anti-backflow valve. Pushing down on the handle forces air out of the side vents—not into the patient's airway. The pulling motion is what creates the powerful suction to pull the object out safely.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "collapsible-row-content",
          "settings": {
            "open": false,
            "heading": "Can the device be reused after an emergency?",
            "icon": "check_box",
            "filled_icon": false,
            "row_content": "<p><br/>The main suction body is durable and reusable. However, for sanitary reasons and to ensure maximum effectiveness, we strongly recommend replacing the masks after they have been used in a real emergency situation.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_1",
        "faq_2",
        "faq_3",
        "faq_4",
        "faq_5",
        "faq_6"
      ],
